<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gustav IV Adolf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1778">1778</a>–<a href="/years/1837">1837</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Gustavus IV Adolphus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gustav IV Adolf was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> from 1792 to 1809. A determined enemy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>, he joined the coalitions against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, abolished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serfdom">serfdom</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Swedish Pomerania</a> in 1806 and lost the territory to French occupation in 1807. The loss of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1809 led to his deposition in a coup, and he died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gustav-iv-adolf.jpg" alt="Gustav IV Adolf" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Per Krafft the Younger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gustav_IV_Adolf_of_Sweden.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Wars against Russia in 1741–1743 and 1788–1790 failed to reverse the verdict, and in the Finnish War of 1808–1809 Russia conquered Finland, ceded by the Treaty of Fredrikshamn in 1809; the defeat led to the deposition of <b>Gustav IV Adolf</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-sweden">Kingdom of Sweden · Into the Present</a></li><li><blockquote>Serfdom was abolished in 1806 under <b>Gustav IV Adolf</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/swedish-pomerania">Swedish Pomerania</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Stockholm Palace, in what is now <a href="/countries/sweden">Sweden</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-gallen">St. Gallen</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/switzerland">Switzerland</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=59.33,18.07&amp;year=1816" aria-label="Stockholm Palace on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4931 170 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Gustav IV Adolf"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5381 440h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5381 440h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=59.33,18.07&amp;year=1816">What was here in 1816? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
